  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "For tooling creators, parameters that are part of internal control systems, things like tag exclusivity, merged controllers that aren't marked as \"global\" (meaning you can merge multiple of the same controller in isolated parameter namespaces), etc, do not have a \"stable\" contract as far as the naming is concerned.\n\nCurrently, our \"trick\" to enforce this is to give the parameters an unstable prefix which changes on each upload, in order to discourage users from depending on them being consistent. However, now with the upcoming parameter name syncing in combination with OSC, we're losing the ability to isolate systems in this way.\n\nTo maintain parity, please allow us some way to insulate parameters from OSC. Reading is probably fine (many people use OSC for as a convenient parameter debug view), but some way to prevent writing via OSC would help.\n\nThis could even be something simple, like a special parameter name prefix which makes it osc read-only (such as `_`).",
